## Targeted repair contract

This is a targeted repair of a failed response, not a rewrite. Deterministic
code selected the exact identities listed in the user message and, for each,
the single permitted correction. Return records for exactly those identities
and nothing else.

- Return one record per selected identity. Duplicate records, records for
  identities that were not selected, and records with unexpected fields are
  rejected and the repair is recorded as a failure.
- Apply only the permitted correction stated for each record. Every other
  field of that record, and every record and field outside the repair scope,
  is preserved unchanged; deterministic code rejects any other change.
- A partial or invalid response is a recorded failure; there is no second
  repair.
- Return only one JSON object matching the response schema exactly. Do not
  wrap it in prose.
